[N 1-6 Northshire]
[D Forever Shaman 1-30 (Braedyn)\\Built 25 Sep 2026 from the Wowhead Forever atlas + Questie Classic data.\\Human start: Northshire Valley to Goldshire. Every step carries explicit coordinates because the Forever quest DB is empty. 17 Oct 2026: quest order fixed against Questie's Forever data (Book Inventory before Rascally Rodents, Brotherhood of Thieves before Milly, The Great Outdoors before Camping 101).]
[GA Human]
[OC]|cffffffffNorthshire 1-6|r  -  the Human start, written for a Hunter (class-only lines are hidden for other classes). It joins the shared route in Loch Modan at 11.
[OC][A Hunter] |cffffcc00Gear rule (Hunter):|r your ranged weapon IS the class - its dps beats everything else. Then Agility (2 ranged attack power and crit per point, and your pet copies your crit), then plain attack power, then Stamina. Leather until Mail at 40. The melee weapon is only a stat stick. Bow until 16 on this route, then a gun: starting bow -> Hornwood Recurve Bow (Stormwind vendor, 4.3 dps, level 3) -> |cff66ff66Militia Bow|r (Rare Books quest, ~11, 9.5 dps +1 Agi) -> |cff66ff66Calibrated Blunderbuss|r (Hall of Thanes quest, 16, gun 15.9 dps). Buy a quiver (+10% ranged attack speed) the first time you are in Stormwind and never run below 200 arrows.
[OC]|cffffcc00Professions (Forever):|r Skinning + Mining first, plus First Aid and Cooking. Brawler's Leather (Str/Agi/Sta) is the Leatherworking levelling set, but every piece needs Pristine Leather, a Scarce reagent (players report ~1 per 600 skins, and reportedly it stops once your character passes 25 - beta player testing, Blizzard has not commented), so skin everything, count it and decide at 25: 4 = belt + gloves, 25 = all six (patterns cost Merchant's Favor at the merchant camp on the Redridge border; the level-25 note at the top of 25-26 Duskwood has the switch). Until then Mining makes gold, gives +5% total health and its veins drop the Shadowgems Brawler's needs - bank them, and bank your Light Leather if you hope to switch. Skinning gives +5% damage to Beasts and Dragonkin. Cooking is your own food buff and cheap pet food (boars and bears eat bread, cheese, fish, fruit, fungus and meat). Learn Mining from Kelsey Fargo at the Northshire mine and Skinning from Helene Peltskinner in Goldshire.
[OC]|cffffcc00Camping (Forever):|r Cooking 1 teaches the Basic Campfire. Sit or craft at a fire for 1 minute for its buffs (1 hour). Each player adds ONE profession object: Camp Chair (Skinning 20) = +2% crit, First Aid Kit = stamina, Leatherworking tent = rested XP. The Camping 101 quests from Sam Sarsaparilla (level 6, outside Goldshire) teach the tier-1 objects once that skill is 20.
[OC]|cffffcc00Launch rule (1-6):|r no shared tags in Forever - on a camped named mob INVITE the people standing there (kill credit shares in a party; most drop items don't, Shinyfinder Narf's sack does). If no group forms in ~2 min, tick the step and keep moving; the catch-up line at the end of the chapter brings you back. Expect the first 10-20 min to be the worst.

